  "nl_text": "The rschema_0224 database is designed to manage user information and task-related data. The database contains five tables: user, task, task_execution_status, user_quote, and user_evaluation. The user table stores information about each user, including their unique identifier, name, avatar URL, contact information, the number of failed tasks, and the number of completed tasks. The task table holds details about each task, such as its unique identifier, title, description, budget, deadline, category, and address. The task_execution_status table tracks the progress of each task, linking it to the user who is executing the task and the task itself, with the relationship between the task executor and the task being a many-to-one relationship. The user_quote table stores quotes from users for specific tasks, linking the user who made the quote, the task, the quote itself, and any additional comments. The user_evaluation table contains records of user evaluations, including the unique identifier for the evaluation, the evaluator and executor of the task, and the rating given, with both the evaluator and executor being linked to the user table.",
  "gold_question": "The online task publishing and management system shall allow users to register and maintain personal information, including avatars and contact details. Users shall be able to publish tasks in the system, specifying the task title, description, budget, and deadline, and assigning the task to a specific category, city, or location. Other users shall be able to respond to published tasks, providing quotes and additional comments. After the task publisher selects an executor, both parties shall be able to communicate through messages within the system, exchange relevant files, and track task progress. Upon task completion, the publisher shall be able to evaluate the executor and provide ratings. The system shall also support managing basic user statistics, such as the number of completed tasks and failed tasks, to help other users better understand the reliability of executors. By associating cities, locations, categories, and tasks, the system shall effectively help users match suitable tasks with executors, improving task completion efficiency.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0224.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0224\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar_url` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `failed_tasks` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `completed_tasks` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `budget` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deadline` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_execution_status` (\n  `status_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`status_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_execution_status_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `task_execution_status_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_quote` (\n  `quote_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quote` text NOT NULL,\n  `comments` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`quote_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_quote_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_quote_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_evaluation` (\n  `evaluation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `evaluator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `executor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`evaluation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`evaluator_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_evaluation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`executor_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_evaluation_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`task_id`) REFERENCES `task` (`task_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
